  "preamble": "Monophthongization is a sound change where a diphthong simplifies into a single, stable vowel sound. This process often reduces articulatory effort and can be found in the historical development of languages like French and various dialects of English. In Middle Indo-Aryan the Sanskrit diphthong au became o (gaura > Shauraseni gora, mauktika > Prakrit mottia).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Monophthongization, Rounding, Height Adjustment",
